cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EchoPlane3D, please cite it as below, and cite SAM 2 and the CAMUS dataset if you use them."
title: "EchoPlane3D: an open-source, offline split-screen workbench coupling video foundation models with 3D cardiac plane slicing for echocardiography training"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
10.5281/zenodo.24377991
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
authors:
  -   family-names: "Zaim"
    given-names: "Burhan"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Medicine and Health, Al-Farabi Kazakh National University, Almaty, Kazakhstan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zaimzoy2004-gif/EchoPlane3D"
keywords:
  - echocardiography
  - education
  - Simpson's method of disks
  - left ventricular ejection fraction
  - apical foreshortening
  - SAM 2
  - Three.js
abstract: >-
  EchoPlane3D is an offline teaching and research workbench that links a 2-D echocardiography clip,
  segmented and tracked with the SAM 2.1 video foundation model and quantified with the 20-disk
  method of disks, to a 3-D cardiac model sliced along the standard echocardiographic planes, including
  an interactive simulation of apical foreshortening. It is a research prototype, not a medical device.
